<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen Jan-Mar trade deficit narrows to $20.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Turkmen Jan-Mar trade deficit narrows to $20.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan posted a trade deficit of $20.3 million in the first three months of this year compared to a $28.8 million in the same period of 1996, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>    TURKMEN MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jan-Mar 97  Jan-Mar 96</p>
<p>    Exports($ million)		   64.3	  80.8</p>
<p>    Imports($ million)		   84.6	 109.6</p>
<p>    Trade balance($ million)	  -20.3	 -28.8</p>
<p>Notes -- The figures do not include trade with the Commonwealth of Independent States. Including CIS countries, Turkmenistan posted a trade surplus of $67.0 million in the first quarter of this year.</p>
<p>	  --Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
